\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Hark! The song of jubilee,
\par Loud as mighty thunders' roar:
\par Or the fullness of the sea,
\par When it breaks upon the shore.
\par Hallelujah! For the Lord
\par God Omnipotent shall reign:
\par Hallelujah! Let the word
\par Echo round the earth and main.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Hallelujah! Hark! The sound,
\par From the depths unto the skies,
\par Wakes above, beneath, around,
\par All creation's harmonies:
\par See Jehovah's banner furled:
\par Sheathed His sword; He speaks-'tis done:
\par And the kingdoms of this world
\par Are the kingdoms of His Son.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He shall reign from pole to pole 
\par With illimitable sway:
\par He shall reign, when, like a scroll,
\par Yonder heavens have passed away:
\par Then the end- beneath His rod
\par Man's last enemy shall fall;
\par Hallelujah! Christ in God,
\par God in Christ, is All in all.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

